## Statement

Let $A$ and $B$ be subsets of a set $E$. Prove that
$$E\setminus(A\cup B)=(E\setminus A)\cap(E\setminus B).$$

## Hint

Take an element $x$ of $E$ and translate "$x\notin A\cup B$" using logic.

## Solution

Let $x\in E$. Then
$$x\in E\setminus(A\cup B)\iff x\notin A\cup B\iff \text{not}\,(x\in A\text{ or }x\in B)\iff x\notin A\text{ and }x\notin B.$$

The last statement means $x\in E\setminus A$ and $x\in E\setminus B$, that is $x\in(E\setminus A)\cap(E\setminus B)$. The two sets have the same elements, so they are equal.
